A||N||12||chris6878||New Dash Speakers.... ?||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||05-18-2000||04:05 PM||||I just recently purchased a new set of pyramid 4x10's, 3-way, 250 watts each. Just with my cd player alone with no amp, they dont sound any  better than my radio shack 4x10's. I guess an amp would fix this huh?    oh yeah.. how do ya know which is + or - on the speakers?         I am not a stereo finatic, so i dont know these things..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>TIA,<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||Homicidal||05-18-2000||04:11 PM||||If you don't know + or -, it might be best to have someone else install the speakers.<P>As for sounding better, they usually don't really shine better until you get into the loud volume ranges.<P>I bet you bought those off Ebay, I was going to get some also!  I still am.  They should compliment my 10" sub nicely!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||05-18-2000||04:41 PM||||yep...  ebay is where i got em...    $40 shipping and all...||||reg||12
Z||000003||Homicidal||05-18-2000||05:22 PM||||They would go so nicely in my system.<P>Did you know Pyramid is actually Pioneer?  Yah, they are Pioneer's lower end speaker company since Pioneer bought them out!<P>Anyways, let me know how they work out, I think I might pick up a pair.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||05-18-2000||10:53 PM||||I peeked under my grills and found a pair of the Pyramids that the previous owner had installed.I wanted to know what I was going to blow with the Higher powered pioneer deck I was installing,funny how it sounds alright together.I didn't know that about the brand/marketing thing between the two companies.<BR>Oh,almost forgot,the red terminal is usually positive.<p>[This message has been edited by lowCG (edited 05-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||LarryB||05-18-2000||11:47 PM||||With loudspeakers it doesn't matter which end is + or -, as long as you wire the speakers all the same way.<P>If you wire them the same way they will be in phase, if you reverse one they will be out of phase, i.e. the cone of 1 speaker will be moving in while the cone of the other speaker will be moving out. Speakers that are out of phase sound terrible. <P>Pyramids are designed to be sold at the $40 price point.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||chris6878||05-19-2000||01:05 AM||||I noticed the speakers have a little red sticker beside the positive. Duh.. i should have seen this earlier...     <P>I didnt know about the pyramid buyout either, now i need an amp to put on these speakers...<P>thanks for the replies,<BR>chris||||reg||3
Z||000008||Oreif||05-19-2000||01:24 AM||||On car speakers (coaxial/triaxial) you cannot hook the positive and negative backwards. The crossover capacitor (or network on some) is hooked to the positive side of the speaker. Hooking them up backwards will fry the tweeter section over time. ||||reg||4
Z||000009||Racer 1||05-19-2000||01:52 AM||||If you wire the speakers backwards the voice coil will hit the back of the magnet plate if powered by a amp?||||reg||4
Z||000010||Homicidal||05-19-2000||02:02 AM||||Just find out which is + and which is - and you won't have ANY of these problems!!<P>bad problem but simple solution!||||reg||1
Z||000011||dragnlo||05-19-2000||10:13 AM||||I agree with LarryB it does not matter if you wire them out of phase as long as all of the speakers(playing the same frequency range) are out of phase. <P>The polarity only changes the time in which you hear the sound. So if one speaker is out of phase instead of increasing volume(outputs sine waves at same time), like you would think when you have more than one speaker. It will decrease your volume(by shifting one of the sine waves 180 degrees out of phase). Yes you will still be able to hear the speaker if it is out of phase, it just wont be as loud as it should be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <BR>And about the voice coil thing, the voice coil can hit the magnet plate whether they are in phase or out of phase. That depends on how much power you are giving them through an amp. <P>Hope this helps and sorry for the long post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>dragnlo||||reg||1
Z||000012||Phil||05-19-2000||12:24 PM||||Just got my 4x10 3way from JC Whitney 29.95 today and they were Pyramids. Plus you get an extra 10% off||||reg||1
Z||000013||DRH||05-19-2000||02:29 PM||||Tip for finding speaker polarity if they aren't marked... Get a 1.5 volt battery (AAA, AA, C, D cell) and a couple of short pieces of wire. Touch the wires to the battery and the speaker and watch the cone. <P>When the battery + is attached to the speaker + the cone will move OUT. If it is reversed it will move IN.<P>I have heard that polarity is important for bass. Otherwise the speaker is "pulling" rather than "pushing" when the amp "hits"... That theory is supported by what happens in the test above.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
